1.2  Material 3  --  crates/teksilo-theme-material3
---------------------------------------------------------------------------

The baseline token values -- the static Material 3 reference scheme derived
from the canonical seed #6750A4, the M3 type ramp, and the state-layer and
disabled-state opacities -- are read from Google's published Material
Design 3 specification. Google publishes that documentation under the
Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International License and its code samples
under the Apache License 2.0. No Material Design source code is included,
and no text or image is copied from the documentation.

    Source: https://m3.material.io/
    Content license: https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/
    Site policies: https://developers.google.com/site-policies

    Material Design is published by Google LLC.


1.3  macOS Aqua and Dark Aqua  --  crates/teksilo-theme-macos
---------------------------------------------------------------------------

Apple publishes very little of the numeric detail this preset needs. Every
literal in the crate is tagged at its definition as [HIG] (published on
developer.apple.com), [measured] (observed from a running system), or
[derived] (computed by Teksilo). Published metrics and measurements are
facts rather than licensed material; Apple grants no licence over them and
none is claimed here. No Apple source code, artwork, icon, or font is
included. San Francisco is named under an off-by-default Cargo feature and
is never embedded.


1.4  Int UI  --  crates/teksilo-core/src/presets/intui.rs
---------------------------------------------------------------------------

Teksilo's default token set is an independent implementation informed by
JetBrains' published Int UI design language. No JetBrains source code,
resource file, or artwork is included, and no token value is transcribed
from one.


1.5  KDE Plasma / Breeze  --  crates/teksilo-kde-scheme, crates/teksilo-theme-kde
---------------------------------------------------------------------------

teksilo-kde-scheme reads the files a KDE Plasma desktop keeps its look in:
the KConfig text format and its cascade, the KDE colour-scheme model, Qt's
font descriptions and the related desktop settings. Its behaviour is
re-implemented from Teksilo's own written specification,
engineering/docs/kde-breeze-spec.md, which describes KDE's formats, rules
and values in prose. No KDE or Qt source code is included in Teksilo, and
none was copied or translated: the specification was written from the
upstream sources by one author, and the code is written from the
specification alone. Values such as default colours and numeric constants
are facts; the specification's ledger records, for each one, the upstream
file and line it was observed in.

teksilo-theme-kde, the KDE Plasma theme preset, builds Teksilo themes from
those colour schemes and transcribes the Breeze design language from the
same specification: the widget style's metrics, painting rules and motion,
and the Kirigami units it relies on. Each value is tagged at its definition
with where it was observed ([M], [S] and [Hp] for the Breeze widget style,
[K] for Kirigami, [Qd] for the desktop QtQuick style, [qt] for Qt's public
documentation, [measured-qt] for the Qt runtime) or how Teksilo derived it
([derived], [wcag], [unpublished]). Where a stock Breeze colour falls short
of WCAG, the theme lifts it by a stated rule and says so. No KDE or Qt
source code, artwork, icon or font is included in it.

The specification describes these upstream releases:

    plasma/breeze                   v6.8.0
    plasma/plasma-workspace         v6.8.0
    plasma/plasma-integration       v6.8.0
    plasma/xdg-desktop-portal-kde   v6.8.0
    frameworks/kconfig              v6.31.0
    frameworks/kcolorscheme         v6.31.0
    frameworks/kguiaddons           v6.31.0
    frameworks/kirigami             v6.31.0
    frameworks/qqc2-desktop-style   v6.31.0
    qt/qtbase                       v6.11.1  (the Qt runtime observed)

    Source: https://invent.kde.org/

KDE publishes its colour and configuration libraries under the GNU Lesser
General Public License (Plasma's colour-scheme settings under version 2.0
only) and the Breeze widget style under the GNU General Public License,
as stated in each upstream file. Teksilo takes no code under either
licence.

Test fixtures. Three stock Breeze colour schemes from plasma/breeze v6.8.0
are vendored verbatim, so the tests can compare Teksilo's constants
