===========================================================================
3. FONTS NAMED BUT NOT REDISTRIBUTED
===========================================================================

Three theme presets can ask the platform's text stack for a system face by
name, under their "system-fonts" feature. The face resolves only on a
machine that already has it installed; on any other, the text stack falls
back to the bundled Inter and JetBrains Mono.

The Microsoft and Apple faces are proprietary. Neither is included in this
repository or in any binary built from it, and no licence to either is
granted or implied.

    Segoe UI Variable, Consolas    Microsoft Corporation
                                   teksilo-theme-fluent, "system-fonts"

    SF Pro Text, SF Mono           Apple Inc.
                                   teksilo-theme-macos, "system-fonts"

Noto Sans and Hack, KDE Plasma's default faces, are free fonts, the
releases in 2.6 and 2.7. Under "system-fonts" alone teksilo-theme-kde
embeds neither and uses the copies installed on the machine, under the
licences they were installed with; only its "bundled-fonts" feature
embeds them.

    Noto Sans, Hack                The Noto Project Authors; Source Foundry
                                   Authors and Bitstream, Inc.
                                   teksilo-theme-kde, "system-fonts"

The same applies to the platform colour-emoji faces (Noto Color Emoji, Apple
Color Emoji, Segoe UI Emoji) that the teksilo-text "system-emoji" feature
reads from well-known paths at startup: located at runtime, never embedded.


